1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Antoinette Corisande Élisabeth, Duchess of Clermont-Tonnerre (née. de Gramont; 23 April 1875 – 6 December 1954) was a French writer of the early 20th century, best known for her long-term lesbian relationship with 
2 CONC Natalie Clifford Barney, an American writer. Élisabeth de Gramont had grown up among the highest aristocracy; when she was a child, according to Janet Flanner, "peasants on her farm... begged her not to clean her shoes before ente
2 CONC ring their houses". She looked back on this lost world of wealth and privilege with little regret, and became known as the "red duchess" for her support of socialism and feminism.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a close friend, and sometimes critic of writer Marcel Proust, whom she had first met on 9 June 1903.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%89lisabeth_de_Gramont
